If API permissions are missing for your React app in Azure AD B2C, follow these steps to fix it:


---

1. Check If API is Registered Correctly

1. Go to Azure Portal → Azure AD B2C → App registrations.


2. Select your Web API app registration (e.g., MyB2CApi).


3. Go to Expose an API.


4. Ensure the Application ID URI is set (e.g., https://yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com/api).


5. Check if at least one scope exists (e.g., access_api).

If missing:

Click Add a scope.

Name it access_api.

Set Admin consent description: Allows access to My API.

Click Save.





---

2. Add API Permissions to React App

1. Go to Azure AD B2C → App registrations.


2. Select your React app (MyReactApp).


3. Navigate to API Permissions → Add a permission.


4. Click My APIs → Select MyB2CApi.


5. Select the scope access_api.


6. Click Add permissions.


7. Click Grant admin consent to apply changes.




---

3. Verify MSAL Configuration in React

Check authConfig.js:

const msalConfig = {
  auth: {
    clientId: "YOUR_REACT_APP_CLIENT_ID",
    authority: "https://yourtenant.b2clogin.com/YOUR_TENANT_NAME.onmicrosoft.com/B2C_1A_SIGNUP_SIGNIN",
    knownAuthorities: ["yourtenant.b2clogin.com"],
    redirectUri: "http://localhost:3000",
  },
};

const loginRequest = {
  scopes: ["https://yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com/api/access_api"],
};


---

4. Clear Cache & Restart

1. In Azure Portal, go to App registrations → MyReactApp.


2. Click Manage > Manifest and check that the requiredResourceAccess includes your API.


3. Clear browser cache & local storage.


4. Restart the React app:

npm start




---

This should fix the missing permissions issue. If you still face problems, let me know what error you're getting!

